{"agent":"n2-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"budget_forced":"the fixes made after critic reviewed are now on the tree; re-review them","chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"With `[lease].reconcile_tests` at its specified default `affected`, a complete is cleared by any post-`at` `unit_tests` or `ci` pass whose `evidence.tree_sha` merely starts with the 12-char main prefix. The knob text in `knob_added.lease.reconcile_tests.toml` defines `affected` as the tests the reconciled files select, and the governing note refuses complete until those affected tests passed on the reconciled tree. Given `reconciled={files:[\"pkg/a.py\"], main:\"abcdef0123456789\", at:\"2026-10-17T00:00:00Z\"}` and a `ci` pass at a later stamp with `tree_sha=\"abcdef012345+clean\"` and no file selection, line 332 sets `passed` and the function returns `\"\"`, so complete proceeds even though the affected tests for `pkg/a.py` never ran. The inverse is also wrong: a gate that did run only the tests selected by `pkg/a.py` is never consulted, so that pass cannot clear the guard. The refusal string always tells the operator to run `unit_tests`, which is the full suite, not the affected set.","digest":"c7b5fa02bdbc082a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/completion/rules.py:330","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/completion/rules.py:330"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The required evidence is a suite run that names the reconciled files. `names_reconciled_tree` ignores every evidence field except `tree_sha`, and the comment states the note is never consulted. Given `reconciled.files=[\"src/lease.py\"]` and a `unit_tests` PASSED record at or after `at` whose evidence is only `{tree_sha: \"<main-prefix>+clean\"}` with no reconciled path, `passed_on_reconciled_tree` is true and `_reconciled_blocker` returns `\"\"`, so complete is allowed without evidence naming `src/lease.py`.","digest":"698a9ebe21de6980","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/completion/rules.py:314","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/completion/rules.py:314"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_a_reconciled_merge_with_a_passed_ci_completes` clears the reconcile blocker for a `ci` pass whose evidence is only the prose `affected tests on the reconciled tree: tests/test_x.py (reached by src/x.py)`. That string does not name the reconciled commit (`base`/`main` are HEAD). The governing note requires the affected tests to have passed on the reconciled tree, and the later tests in this file reject path-substring notes and `tree_sha` values that do not start with the reconciled SHA. Given that evidence, this test requires the guard to drop, so a pre-reconcile run whose note merely mentions `src/x.py` is accepted as proof.","digest":"2af9017b3f10a626","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_lease_reconcile_merge.py:77","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_lease_reconcile_merge.py:77"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`test_a_missing_base_sha_records_an_unknown_reconcile_fail_closed` only asserts `reconciled[\"unknown\"]` and that `src/x.py` is listed. It never calls `CM.verdict`. An empty `base_sha` that stamps `unknown` but does not refuse complete still passes, so the fail-closed contract is not locked.","digest":"63f29a7cf2af7899","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_lease_reconcile_merge.py:259","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_lease_reconcile_merge.py:259"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":24590,"diff_sha":"fbdf03c6134900cfeef9214a2c8a5f7ad9ad3a3d79bb12525fdd50f4d51a7201","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/B-lease-reconcile-merge","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":67.0,"family":"xai","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"cf45fbdf29a2b9b5","output_file":