{"agent":"n2-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The lease filter was removed, so autoformat still stages files outside the item's globs. Previously `owned` kept only paths matching `it.globs`. Now it is every path from `changed_python(..., own=True)`. Three-dot only drops files `base` introduced; it does not enforce the lease. Given an item whose globs are `src/a.py` and a commit that also edits unformatted `src/b.py`, `base...sha` returns both, `auto_fix` rewrites and stages `src/b.py`, and the outside-lease collision this bug names still happens.","digest":"3b4681f7b847c15a","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/cirun.py:130","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/cirun.py:130"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The replacement test never runs the hook, so it does not lock the stated regression. It only asserts `changed_python(own=True) == [\"src/a.py\"]` on a throwaway repo. It does not call `cirun.run` / `auto_fix`, and it never checks that an unformatted file outside the item's changes is left unstaged. A hook that still formats and stages `src/b.py` (the old glob case, or any path that ignores `owned`) passes this test.","digest":"e559849d04e3ea34","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_ci_ruff.py:123","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_ci_ruff.py:123"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":2,"delta_from":"8e94e52338c84cd75c96c08ed62714f10000e015","delta_raised":["3b4681f7b847c15a","e559849d04e3ea34"],"delta_rounds":2,"diff_chars":4825,"diff_sha":"e7a40603fdbfa68a04b5f306b2c48a131b95c34adb6c4f8f5203f0b98601c162","diff_source":"commit 8e94e52338c8 vs its first parent","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":75.3,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"5aed495138d277ff","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-autoformat-stages-outside-