{"agent":"n2-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The help and docstring promise a diff/plan mode that reports what `refresh_docs` would rewrite, but nothing here computes a diff or compares content. `_plan_driver` at least classifies create/current/refuse/rewrite; `_plan_block` reads `existing` and is passed `section`, then ignores both and always returns \"would refresh the managed block in {label}\". `_plan_native` never opens the rule file and always returns \"would refresh the native rule for {key}\". Given an adopted repo whose AGENTS.md managed block already equals `section`, and a native rule that already matches the template, `refresh_docs(..., plan=True)` still lists both as refreshes and shows none of the bytes that a hand-edited driver would lose to `.local-edits`. An operator cannot tell a no-op from the B420810120e clobber, which is the case this mode was added to preview.","digest":"89ee9509055572d3","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/adopt/_docs.py:_plan_block","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/adopt/_docs.py:_plan_block"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The managed stamp sha is rewritten from `0be24948b488` to `a63ce4b4bf30` while this diff does not change the region body. `content_digest` is taken from that body (`stamp.sha == content_digest(view, ...)` in the new test and the existing driver-drift check), so a body-identical view still digests to the old sha. Given the post-change file, `region.stamp(...).sha` is `a63ce4b4bf30` and `content_digest(view)` is still `0be24948b488`, so the stamp no longer certifies the body and `test_claude_delta_carries_the_lane_context_caps_section` fails on the change that was meant to close B420810120e.","digest":"ff6feffc60be832b","family":"xai","location":"docs/ddflow/drivers/deltas/claude-code.md:1","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"docs/ddflow/drivers/deltas/claude-code.md:1"}],"chunks_total":